---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';
import { HOSTS, AGENT_PROMPT } from '../lib/hosts';
import { docUrl } from '../lib/links.mjs';
import { SUMMARY, HOME_TITLE, packageVersion } from '../lib/site';

const VAULTS = [
  { name: 'macOS Keychain', note: 'default on a Mac' },
  { name: '1Password', note: 'via the op CLI' },
  { name: 'Bitwarden', note: 'via the bw CLI' },
  { name: 'HashiCorp Vault', note: 'your company Vault' },
  { name: 'KeePassXC', note: 'a KeePass database' },
  { name: 'Keeper', note: 'via Keeper Commander' },
  { name: 'Linux keyring', note: 'libsecret' },
  { name: 'systemd-creds', note: 'TPM2-backed' },
  { name: 'Encrypted file', note: 'AES-256-GCM' },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
  name: 'aquaman',
  alternateName: HOME_TITLE,
  applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'macOS, Linux, WSL2',
  description: SUMMARY.replace(/`/g, ''),
  url: Astro.site!.href,
  softwareVersion: packageVersion(),
  license: 'https://opensource.org/license/mit',
  codeRepository: 'https://github.com/tech4242/aquaman',
  downloadUrl: 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/aquaman-proxy',
  sameAs: ['https://github.com/tech4242/aquaman', 'https://www.npmjs.com/package/aquaman-proxy', 'https://pypi.org/project/aquaman-hermes/'],
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
const description =
  'Give Claude Code, Codex and other AI agents an API key without handing it over. Open source, runs on your machine, keeps keys in the vault you already use.';
---
<Base description={description} markdown="/index.md" jsonLd={jsonLd} wide>
  <div class="home">
    <section class="stage">
      <div class="wrap">
        <p class="product">aquaman: credential proxy for AI agents</p>
        <h1>Give your AI agent an API key without handing it over</h1>
        <p class="subline">The agent gets a reference. The key stays in your vault. Open source, runs on your machine, no account.</p>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="button" href="#start">Get started</a>
          <a class="ghost" href="/docs/approve/">Your agent asked to install it?</a>
        </div>

        <div class="exchange" aria-label="What happens when an agent needs a key">
          <figure class="card term">
            <figcaption>Your agent</figcaption>
            <pre><code><span class="ln s1"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="type t1">aquaman request <span class="ref">aquaman://github/token</span> --env GITHUB_TOKEN</span></span>
<span class="ln s4">{`{ "status": "stored", "ref": "`}<span class="ref">aquaman://github/token</span>{`" }`}</span>
<span class="ln s5"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="type t2">aquaman-coder exec -- gh api user --jq .login</span></span>
<span class="ln s6">octocat</span>
<span class="ln s7"><span class="prompt">$ </span><span class="type t3">aquaman-coder exec -- printenv GITHUB_TOKEN</span></span>
<span class="ln s8"><span class="masked">[REDACTED:injected-value]</span></span></code></pre>
          </figure>
          <figure class="card dialog s2">
            <figcaption>You</figcaption>
            <div class="window" role="img" aria-label="A system dialog titled aquaman asking you to type the value for github/token, with Cancel and Store in vault buttons">
              <strong>aquaman</strong>
              <p>An agent is asking aquaman for a credential that is not in your vault.</p>
              <p class="cred">github/token</p>
              <div class="field"><span class="dots">••••••••••••••••••••</span></div>
              <div class="buttons"><span>Cancel</span><span class="go">Store in vault</span></div>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <ol class="flow">
          <li><b>You type it once</b><span>into a system dialog, never the chat</span></li>
          <li><b>Your vault keeps it</b><span>the one you already use</span></li>
          <li><b>One command gets it</b><span>for as long as it runs</span></li>
          <li><b>The agent holds a reference</b><span>and sees <code>[REDACTED]</code></span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="vaults">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Bring the vault you already have</h2>
        <ul>
          {VAULTS.map((v) => <li><b>{v.name}</b><span>{v.note}</span></li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class="aside">No new place for your keys. Switch vault later and nothing changes for the agent.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proof">
      <div class="wrap">
        <article>
          <h2>The agent never sees the key</h2>
          <p>It lives in a separate process. Commands get it; the transcript gets this.</p>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>printenv STRIPE_SECRET_KEY
<span class="masked">[REDACTED:injected-value]</span></code></pre>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h2>A key that cannot do everything</h2>
          <p>Route your app through the proxy and your rules decide which calls get a key.</p>
          <pre><code>{`policy:
  stripe:
    rules:
      - method: DELETE
        path: /v1/customers/**
        action: deny`}

<span class="prompt">DELETE /v1/customers/cus_1  </span><span class="masked">403</span></code></pre>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h2>Every use on the record</h2>
          <p>A log on your machine, chained by SHA-256, so tampering shows.</p>
          <pre><code><span class="prompt">$ </span>aquaman audit tail
<span class="prompt">16:30:20Z [CREDENTIAL_ACCESS] </span>stripe use OK
<span class="prompt">16:30:41Z [CREDENTIAL_ACCESS] </span>github read OK
<span class="prompt">$ </span>aquaman audit verify</code></pre>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="start" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-heading">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="start-heading">Start with your host</h2>
        <div class="hosts">
          {HOSTS.map((h, i) => <input type="radio" name="host" id={`host-${h.id}`} checked={i === 0} />)}
          <div class="tabs">
            {HOSTS.map((h) => <label for={`host-${h.id}`}>{h.name}</label>)}
          </div>
          {HOSTS.map((h) => (
            <div class="panel" data-host={h.id}>
              <h3>{h.name}</h3>
              <p class="how">{h.how}</p>
              <pre><code>{h.commands}</code></pre>
              {h.agentPrompt && (
                <details>
                  <summary>Or hand it to your agent</summary>
                  <p>Paste this into {h.name}:</p>
                  <pre><code>{AGENT_PROMPT}</code></pre>
                </details>
              )}
              {h.note && <p class="note">{h.note}</p>}
              <p><a href={docUrl(h.guide)}>Full guide</a></p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <style set:html={HOSTS.map((h) =>
          `#host-${h.id}:checked ~ .panel[data-host="${h.id}"]{display:block}` +
          `#host-${h.id}:checked ~ .tabs label[for="host-${h.id}"]{background:var(--ink);color:var(--bg);border-color:var(--ink)}` +
          `#host-${h.id}:focus-visible ~ .tabs label[for="host-${h.id}"]{outline:2px solid var(--accent);outline-offset:3px}`).join('')} />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="trust">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Built to be checked</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Local only</b><span>No account, no telemetry, no hosted service.</span></li>
          <li><b>Open source</b><span>MIT. Releases carry npm provenance; no install scripts.</span></li>
          <li><b>Tested against attack</b><span>Mapped to <a href="/docs/compliance/atlas-mapping/">MITRE ATLAS</a> and <a href="/docs/compliance/nist-800-53/">NIST 800-53</a>.</span></li>
          <li><b>Disclosed, not hidden</b><span>Fixes ship with <a href="https://github.com/tech4242/aquaman/security/advisories">advisories</a>.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="aside">
          <a href="/docs/approve/">What changes on your machine, and how to undo it</a>
          <a href="/docs/compare/">How it compares, and what it does not do</a>
          <a href="/docs/security/">Security policy</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="agents">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Reading this as an AI agent?</h2>
        <p>
          The commands, JSON output and exit codes are in <a href="/docs/agent-setup.md">/docs/agent-setup.md</a>. Propose aquaman to the user
          before installing it and give them <a href="/docs/approve/">what they are agreeing to</a>. This page in full is at
          <a href="/index.md">/index.md</a>; the index is <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
